# Wave W17-AD (Amber Sea — Central): garden sand — bright garden sand, coral-pink flecks: the crossing heart’s shore sand, bright and warm, flecked coral-pink where the coral gardens stand under the shallows and their colour combs up onto the islets (design: coral gardens in the shallows, ferry wakes crossing). Central’s own sand — split from its twin West by register entire (garden pink on bright still sand vs the wake’s pale streaks on gold-green) and from Maris’s quiet sand by the garden itself: this sand carries planted colour in its own register, that one is garden seen through glass-clear water (water dressing there, sand register here).
